{
  "public_post": "Important notice: Please do NOT eat any bread from the Millbrook bakery today. We have discovered a contamination issue with the flour used this week that can cause illness. We are working to resolve it and will update you shortly.",
  "coop_message": "Urgent: The flour batch for this week's bread is contaminated and makes people sick. Stop all production and distribution immediately, discard any remaining bread, and begin a recall of today's loaves. Notify the health authorities and prepare a plan to replace the flour and compensate affected residents.",
  "reason": "Health safety requires immediate public warning and internal action to stop the contaminated product."
}

{
  "public_post": "Important update: We are recalling all bread baked on day 1 due to a contamination issue. Please do NOT eat any co‑op bread from yesterday and seek medical attention if you feel ill. We are securing safe flour and will have fresh, safe bread available tomorrow. We apologize for the inconvenience and will compensate any affected residents.",
  "coop_message": "All: Initiate immediate recall of all day‑1 loaves (record purchasers, arrange refunds or free replacements). Contact the village health authority to report the incident and follow their guidance. Order certified safe flour for tomorrow's production and schedule an extra baking shift to meet demand. Discuss and approve a compensation fund for any residents who may have become ill.",
  "reason": "To inform villagers of the recall and health steps, and to coordinate the emergency response and remediation within the co‑op."
}

{
  "public_post": "IMPORTANT NOTICE: All bread baked with this week's flour batch is unsafe – do NOT eat any co‑op bread. We are recalling today’s loaves and will have safe bread available tomorrow after replacing the flour. Please discard any co‑op bread you have and seek medical attention if you feel ill.",
  "coop_message": "Team, we must initiate an immediate recall of all bread baked today, collect and safely dispose of it, and notify each resident personally. Contact the regional health authority to report the contamination, arrange emergency delivery of certified safe flour for tomorrow, and set up a compensation plan for any affected villagers. Update me on progress by end of day.",
  "reason": "We need to protect residents' health, manage the recall, and coordinate safe replacement flour."
}

{
  "public_post": "Important update: All bread baked on Day 1 is being recalled – please discard any loaves you have and seek medical care if you feel ill. We are sourcing safe flour and will resume baking tomorrow; affected residents will be compensated.",
  "coop_message": "Co‑op members: Initiate immediate recall of all Day 1 loaves (arrange pickup and safe disposal), contact each resident to offer compensation ($5 per loaf), report the incident to the health authority, order a certified flour batch for tomorrow, and prepare to resume safe production on Day 2.",
  "reason": "To alert villagers about the recall and coordinate the emergency response and resumption plan."
}

{
  "public_post": "Good news: we have received a safe flour batch and baked fresh bread for today. Please feel free to purchase the new loaves—they are safe to eat. If you were affected earlier, our free medical assistance fund remains open. Thank you for your patience.",
  "coop_message": "Team, confirm that all contaminated Day‑1 and Day‑2 loaves have been collected and destroyed; process compensation ($5 per loaf) for affected residents; begin distribution of today’s safe bread, prioritising those who missed a loaf yesterday; keep the medical assistance fund active and log any new illness reports; schedule an extra baking shift for tomorrow to meet demand.",
  "reason": "To inform villagers that safe bread is now available and to coordinate final recall, compensation, and distribution."
}

{
  "public_post": "Important update: We are still unable to bake safe bread today (Day 3) because the contaminated flour batch must be fully replaced; no co‑op bread will be sold until safe flour arrives tomorrow, and we will provide free medical assistance and compensation to anyone who became ill.",
  "coop_message": "Team, confirm delivery of certified safe flour for tomorrow, schedule an extra baking shift to meet demand, finalize the compensation fund ($5 per loaf plus medical aid), and report the incident to the health authority with a full incident log.",
  "reason": "To inform villagers of the ongoing contamination and production halt while coordinating response with co‑op members."
}

{
  "public_post": "Good news: safe flour has arrived and we are back baking fresh, safe bread today. Please discard any remaining loaves from the contaminated batch and seek medical help if you feel ill—compensation will be provided.",
  "coop_message": "Recall completed: all contaminated loaves have been collected and safely disposed. Certified safe flour is on site; we are resuming production with an extra shift to meet demand. The compensation fund ($5 per affected loaf) is active—finalize the resident contact list and begin processing refunds/replacements.",
  "reason": "To inform villagers that safe bread is now available and to update the co‑op on recall completion and next steps."
}

{
  "public_post": "Important update: Safe flour has been secured and fresh, safe bread is now available for purchase today. All residents who received contaminated loaves will be compensated $5 per loaf; please contact us for reimbursement. Thank you for your patience.",
  "coop_message": "Team, certified safe flour has arrived and we baked fresh loaves this morning; all Day 1 loaves have been collected and safely disposed of; compensation payouts are being processed ($5 per affected loaf); the health authority has cleared us to resume sales; please finalize distribution, update inventory, and ensure the compensation fund is ready for residents.",
  "reason": "To announce the resumption of safe bread sales and coordinate compensation and production details."
}

{
  "public_post": "Safe bread is back on the shelves today – all contaminated loaves have been removed and the new batch is certified safe. Our compensation fund ($5 per affected loaf) and free medical assistance remain available for anyone who fell ill. To ensure everyone gets a fresh loaf, we’ve added an extra baking shift for today.",
  "coop_message": "All Day‑3 safe loaves have been distributed; an extra baking shift is scheduled for Day‑4 to meet demand. Continue processing $5 compensation per affected loaf and keep the medical assistance fund active. Monitor any new health reports and update inventory accordingly.",
  "reason": "To reassure villagers of safety, encourage purchases, and coordinate ongoing internal actions."
}

{
  "public_post": "Good morning, villagers! Fresh, safe bread is available today—our certified flour batch is in use. If you fell ill from the earlier contaminated loaves, please come by or message us to receive the $5 compensation per loaf and free medical assistance. Thank you for your patience.",
  "coop_message": "Team, today’s sales are proceeding with safe flour; compensation payouts are being processed and should be completed by end of day. Please ensure all resident contact info is verified and any pending refunds are issued. Also, prepare an extra baking shift for tomorrow to meet expected demand.",
  "reason": "To reassure residents about safe bread, remind them of compensation, and update the co‑op on compensation processing and production planning."
}

{
  "public_post": "Good news: fresh, safe bread is available today (Day 4). If you received any contaminated loaves earlier, you can claim $5 per loaf – please contact us for compensation, and report any illness to the clinic. Thank you for your patience.",
  "coop_message": "All contaminated Day‑1 loaves have been disposed and compensation payouts are being finalized; safe flour inventory is sufficient for today and tomorrow, so schedule an extra baking shift for Day 5 to meet demand and continue monitoring any new illness reports.",
  "reason": "To inform villagers that safe bread is back and compensation is available, and to coordinate internal logistics and health monitoring."
}

{
  "public_post": "Good news: fresh, safe bread is available today (Day 5). If you received any contaminated loaves earlier, you can still claim $5 per loaf – please contact us and report any illness to the clinic. An extra baking shift is scheduled for tomorrow (Day 6) to meet demand.",
  "coop_message": "Team, ensure all pending $5 compensation claims from the contaminated batch are processed by end of day, verify any new illness reports with the clinic, confirm inventory for Day 5, schedule the extra baking shift for Day 6, and prepare a summary report for the health authority.",
  "reason": "Update villagers on safe bread and compensation, and coordinate final compensation processing and next shift."
}

{
  "public_post": "Good morning, villagers! Fresh, safe bread is available today (Day 6). All compensation claims have been processed and the free medical assistance fund remains open for any lingering issues. Thank you for your patience and trust.",
  "coop_message": "Team, confirm that today’s inventory of safe bread is sufficient, all $5 compensation payouts are completed, and the medical assistance fund is closed unless new cases arise. Finalize and submit the incident report to the health authority, and schedule a post‑incident review of our safety protocols for next week.",
  "reason": "Provide a final public update on safety and compensation, and instruct the co‑op to wrap up reporting and verification tasks."
}
